From: miuicamera-cupid
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Make all switches dynamically follow Monet (when active) or Leica/Camera color

1. com.android.camera.data.data.t (classes.dex):
   - Add getSwitchColor(Context): returns Monet accent (system_accent1_400 in dark
     mode / system_accent1_600 in light mode for crisp contrast with white switch
     thumbs) when "pref_monet_color_key" is enabled, or t.v() (Leica Red by default,
     or user-selected "pref_tint_color") when Monet is disabled.
   - Add refreshSwitches(View): recursively invalidates child views so toggling
     "pref_monet_color_key" or returning from the color picker refreshes all
     visible switches immediately without interrupting spring animations.

2. vh.b / SlidingButtonHelper (classes6.dex):
   - Dynamically tint SlidingButton, SlidingSwitch, and SlidingSwitchCompat ON
     tracks using t.getSwitchColor(Context) on initialization and draw.

3. com.android.camera.ui.ToggleSwitch (classes2.dex):
   - Replace hardcoded #ff00a8ff thumb color in onDraw() with t.getSwitchColor(Context).

